DATABASE DESIGN &amp; SQL ASSIGNMENT

Scenario: Gym Membership and Management System

A gym wants a database to manage members, membership plans, memberships, trainers, fitness classes, class bookings,

and payments. Each member has a unique ID, name, email, phone, join date, and city. A member may have multiple

memberships over time, while a membership belongs to one member and uses one membership plan. Some members

may not have any memberships.

Each membership plan has a unique ID, name, duration in months, and price. A plan may be used by many memberships,

while a plan may currently have no memberships. Each trainer has a unique ID, name, specialization, and hire date. A

trainer may teach multiple fitness classes, while a class may have one assigned trainer or no assigned trainer yet.

Each fitness class has a unique ID, name, capacity, and scheduled date/time. Members can book many classes, and each

class can have many members; CLASS_BOOKING records this many-to-many relationship and stores the booking date

and attendance status. Each membership may have no payment or multiple payments. Each payment belongs to one

membership and records its date, amount, method, and status.

